{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PLAN CORRECTED A THIRD TIME. Review #3 BLOCKED with three findings, all verified in source. They\nchange this story from 'translate twelve methods' to 'TRIAGE twelve methods', which is a different\njob.\n\n1. get_parent_map — COPYING CLOUD WOULD BREAK. acli_graph.py:180 uses POST /rest/api/3/search/jql with\n   an opaque nextPageToken CURSOR, and its own docstring records (ticket 8b25, live-proven) that the\n   legacy /rest/api/3/search is RETIRED at HTTP 410 and that sending startAt is REJECTED with HTTP\n   400. That endpoint and pagination model are Cloud-v3 only; DC v2 has POST /rest/api/2/search with\n   OFFSET paging. So my Approach instruction to 'read each Cloud counterpart first' was actively\n   misleading for this method — following it yields a 404/400 against DC. Needs a fresh v2\n   implementation.\n\n2. set_reporter — UNREACHABLE ON DC, so implementing it would be DEAD CODE. Its only call site,\n   dispatch_apply_phases._update_one_apply_reporter, resolves via _jira_account_id_for ->\n   identity.jira_account_id and on None records an 'outbound-reporter-unresolved' alert and RETURNS\n   before client.set_reporter is ever invoked. DC has no accountIds at all (NameIdentity keys on\n   name), so that resolution always misses. The real decision is UPSTREAM — teach the call site DC's\n   name identity, or record reporter sync as unsupported on DC.\n\n   Note this also corrects MY OWN classification from the previous round: I had set_reporter in the\n   'propagates (crashes)' bucket. It cannot crash on DC because it is never called. That is a THIRD\n   failure category I did not have — unreachable-by-call-site — alongside crash and silent\n   degradation.\n\n3. (same root as 1 — the pagination incompatibility, stated separately.)\n\nThe plan now requires a RECORDED VERDICT per member (IMPLEMENT with the DC v2 shape / NOT-APPLICABLE\nvia NotImplementedError / UNREACHABLE-BY-CALL-SITE with the upstream decision named), each backed by\ncall-site evidence rather than by symmetry with Cloud. Two new ACs cover get_parent_map's v2\npagination and set_reporter's upstream decision specifically.\n\nRUNNING TALLY of what the reviewer has corrected in my measurements across three rounds: the count\n(ten -> twelve), the failure mode (mostly-crashes -> mostly-silent), the enforcement mechanism\n(isinstance, which raises TypeError on a non-runtime_checkable Protocol), and now the portability\nassumption (Cloud's implementation is not a template). Every correction made the picture worse and\nthe plan better. I am recording that pattern deliberately: my audits have been confidently wrong\nthree times in a row, and the common thread is that I measured STRUCTURE (what exists, what is\ncalled) without checking SEMANTICS (whether it is reachable, whether the endpoint transfers)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785478552426933001,"uuid":"602dd65a-a00a-423d-bc77-c1b0b4cf3301"}